{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_28","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"cat > collab/yang-clojure/1794422563000-engineer-d1-correspondence-r5.gpt-6.1-terra.findings.md <<'EOF'\n# D1 continuation r5: amended fidelity and static replay pilot\n\nStatus: **partial; the full admission/replay gate is not complete**. This continues the append-only r1–r4 findings, including r4's historical class-strict refusal. Worktree mirror only; no canonical-collab promotion, commit, tagged execution, independent verifier result, or corpus record.\n\n## Fidelity amendment\n\n\"'`yang.correspondence-text/profile` now includes `:fidelity-rule :fixed-jvm-integer-wrappers-v1`, so its content address differs from the r4 class-strict profile. Its numeric comparison permits equal Byte/Short/Integer/Long values via exact `long` comparison; all other admitted numeric leaves require same class and `.equals` (including Double NaN, signed zero and BigDecimal scale). Numeric dispatch occurs before generic `=`. Tests cover all four wrapper pairs, changed numeric coordinates, missing metadata, Long/BigInt, decimal scale, signed zero, NaN, collection kind and map/set iteration order. This is scoped to this experimental JVM profile and does not establish behavior for arbitrary programs.\n\nThe map mismatch path includes the map entry'\"'s actual key; capture failures name fixture, supplied admission scope, ordinal and input. The real-fixture test identifies r4's original mismatch precisely: \"'`:beta-eq-false` forms `[15 2]` metadata entry 2 is `:line`, whose value is Integer before printing and Long after reading, with equal value. The amended capture **was observed to pass** on this fixture; it retains the supplied fresh admission coordinate and all four text captures. It does not change the historical r4 failure.\n\n## Producer-side static replay and reopen\n\nFor the one `:beta-eq-false` admission, the new test captures the original input, reads the captured text, recompiles, and compares its root, oracle canonical-source-hash, producer-derived site table, C1 metadata, site binding, stamped root/metadata and explicit stamped-to-unstamped correspondence with the original compilation. It validates both row trees and their application coverage; stamping adds two unmarked applications per wrapper, accounted separately from the C1 markers per the post-port cc3 test. It stores input, profile, expectations, and both canonical row closures in a file-backed store, closes and reopens it, checks all retained row bodies, and repeats the comparisons using fetched input/expectations. This runs only static compilation: no tagged machine, trace or verifier result. Test store is deleted after the test and is not durable publication of a corpus record.\n\nCrucial limit: `d1-check-reconstruction!` **shares** `kernel-stamp-sites`, `cc3-oracle-binding` and the oracle source-hash function with the producer. Thus its site table is not an independently re-derived declaration and the check is not an independent verifier or completed r5 gate. The exact executable dependency/expansion closure and runtime/profile compatibility are not pinned; no cross-host claim is made. A per-fixture replay test passes only that fixture and does not establish the entire corpus. The frozen v1 evidence remains unchanged.\n\n## Testing and remaining work\n\nTDD: the amended wrapper/NaN and profile-id tests first failed against the old class-strict implementation; the first replay test failed for missing helper; an attempted stamped-tree coverage assertion then failed because it incorrectly expected wrapper helpers to be marked, and was corrected to the post-port accounting. The diagnostic tests check the original `:line` key and retained scope/ordinal. Exact final test counts and lint appear in the handoff response. Full oracle suite and tagged lanes were not run.\n\nStill required: independently derive the site declarations from compiled argument expressions; retain and pin the executable profile/interpreter/dependency and expansion closure; provide complete stage-specific refusal coverage and actual per-compilation gates for the corpus; retain the real record and recipe, companion and verification result under their proper ownership and bounds. The current successful pilot does not satisfy the r6 checkpoint of *all* gates complete. Row-lane-only remains the D1 restriction.\nEOF'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
